    question_en: "A company is designing a highly available multi-tier web application inside an Amazon VPC across two Availability Zones. The architecture consists of an Application Load Balancer (ALB) in public subnets, Amazon EC2 application instances in private subnets, and an Amazon RDS Multi-AZ database cluster.\n\nDuring security and architecture reviews, the following two requirements are identified:\n1. Inbound traffic from a known malicious IP address (198.51.100.45/32) targeting the public subnets must be blocked before it reaches the ALB.\n2. The RDS database tier must accept inbound MySQL traffic on port 3306 exclusively from the EC2 application instances without managing static IP addresses while maintaining the principle of least privilege, and satisfy Multi-AZ deployment prerequisites.\n\nWhich combination of actions should the solutions architect take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)",
