    question_en: "A company runs a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances hosting an application. A solutions architect must implement an automated monitoring and remediation solution to handle disk space issues. The solution must meet the following requirements:\n- Monitor OS-level disk space utilization on all EC2 instances.\n- When disk space utilization exceeds 85%, automatically execute a script on the affected instance to compress historical application logs and archive them to durable object storage.\n- Minimize long-term storage costs by transitioning the archived logs to a cheaper storage tier after 30 days and permanently deleting them after 365 days.\n- Minimize operational overhead and avoid managing custom cron jobs or credentials on individual instances.\n\nWhich combination of actions should the solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements?",
