    question_en: "A company receives data files uploaded to an Amazon S3 bucket at irregular and unpredictable intervals throughout the day. Each uploaded file is smaller than 100 MB, and processing takes approximately 20 seconds to validate and transform the data. The transformed files are accessed frequently during the first 30 days after creation. After 30 days, the access pattern becomes unpredictable, with some files accessed multiple times a month and others not accessed for months. All transformed data must remain immediately accessible when requested.\n\nA solutions architect needs to design a solution that automatically processes incoming files and minimizes both compute and storage costs with the least operational overhead.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements?",
