    question_en: "A smart manufacturing company operates an IoT sensor network that monitors thousands of industrial robotic arms across its assembly plants. The architecture includes an Auto Scaling group of Amazon EC2 instances running 24/7 to ingest continuous telemetry data, and a separate fleet of EC2 worker instances that run daily nightly batch jobs to analyze sensor anomalies. The batch analytics application is stateless, highly fault-tolerant, and processes data stored in Amazon S3.\n\nThe company's finance team has established a fixed monthly compute budget. The solutions architect must optimize compute costs and implement a mechanism to notify the engineering team via Amazon SNS if the monthly EC2 costs are projected to exceed the budget limit before the billing cycle ends.\n\nWhich combination of recommendations should the solutions architect provide to meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively? (Choose two.)",
