    question_en: "A company runs a web application deployed across multiple AWS Regions. The application architecture relies on Layer 7 path-based routing to direct traffic to different microservices and requires SSL/TLS termination at the load balancing tier. Global users report inconsistent network latency when accessing the application over the public internet. Additionally, during a regional outage, the company needs traffic to be shifted to a healthy Region within seconds, without experiencing delays caused by client DNS caching or TTL expiration. The domain name is managed in Amazon Route 53.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements with the lowest latency and fastest regional failover?",
