    question_en: "A company is developing a new web application that allows globally distributed users to upload large video files that frequently exceed 6 GB in size. The backend application processes metadata and generates upload credentials, while the files themselves must be uploaded directly to Amazon S3 to prevent server bottlenecks. The development team wants to deploy and manage the web application without provisioning or managing the underlying servers, load balancers, and Auto Scaling groups. Additionally, application updates must maintain full capacity and experience zero downtime.\n\nWhich combination of actions should a solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)",
