    question_en: "A company is planning to migrate its on-premises infrastructure to AWS. The on-premises environment consists of 50 TB of unstructured data stored on an NFS file system and a production MySQL relational database that serves critical operations.\n\nThe company requires a dedicated, private network connection with consistent performance between its on-premises data center and AWS. The unstructured file data must be migrated to Amazon S3, and objects must be automatically archived to Amazon S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval after 90 days to reduce storage costs. The database must be migrated to Amazon RDS for MySQL with minimal downtime, and the target database architecture must support automatic failover in the event of an infrastructure failure.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?",
