    question_en: "An organization collects large analytical data files (averaging 25 GB each) generated by client applications distributed globally. The files must be uploaded to an Amazon S3 bucket. The organization has the following requirements:\n- Maximize upload throughput and reduce latency for globally distributed clients uploading large files.\n- For the first 30 days, data files have unpredictable and fluctuating access patterns.\n- After 30 days, files are accessed infrequently (about once per quarter), but must remain accessible with millisecond retrieval times when requested.\n- After 365 days, files must be retained for 7 years for regulatory compliance at the lowest possible storage cost, where a 12-hour retrieval time is acceptable.\n- Prevent uncommitted multipart upload parts from accumulating ongoing storage charges.\n\nWhich combination of actions meets these requirements MOST cost-effectively?",
