    question_en: "A company runs a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances in private subnets across multiple Availability Zones. Application configurations are stored hierarchically in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Whenever a configuration parameter is updated, all EC2 instances must immediately run a local script to reload the configuration without restarting the instances or interrupting active connections. The company's security policy strictly prohibits opening any inbound ports, including SSH (port 22), on the EC2 instances and forbids storing persistent administrative credentials.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?",
