    question_en: "A SaaS analytics vendor, DataSphere Insights, is developing a multi-tenant web application dashboard for enterprise clients. The application frontend is a single-page application (SPA) hosted in an Amazon S3 bucket behind an Amazon CloudFront distribution. Users must be able to sign in using their corporate Google accounts or email credentials. Once authenticated, the SPA must directly query an Amazon DynamoDB table to retrieve real-time user-specific dashboard metrics with single-digit millisecond latency. The architecture must enforce least privilege access so that users can only access their own metric records, and the company strictly prohibits embedding or managing long-term AWS credentials in the client application.\n\nWhich combination of steps should a solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements? (Choose three.)",
