    question_en: "A company runs a batch data-processing application on Amazon EC2 instances. The processing jobs are stateless, fault-tolerant, and can be interrupted and resumed at any time without data loss. The application requires a shared, POSIX-compliant file system that all EC2 instances can access concurrently to read and write processing data. Additionally, the company requires automated daily backups of the shared storage.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements with the LOWEST compute cost and the LEAST operational overhead?",
