    question_en: "A government agency is migrating its public records archiving portal to AWS. The portal processes and stores historical digitized records, municipal documents, and multimedia archives that frequently exceed 5 GB in file size. The agency wants to run the containerized application without the operational overhead of provisioning, patching, or managing underlying virtual servers. The application must securely upload and access records in an Amazon S3 bucket without storing or hardcoding long-term AWS credentials inside the container image or task definition. Additionally, the solution must reliably support uploading files larger than 5 GB while preventing unexpected storage costs from failed or abandoned uploads.\n\nWhich combination of actions should a solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)",
