    question_en: "An organization is designing an architecture to process transaction events received via an API. Three independent backend services must each receive and process a copy of every transaction event. The backend services process data at different rates, and one service occasionally experiences processing delays during peak traffic hours. A solutions architect must design a solution that completely decouples the services, buffers incoming requests to handle processing delays, and prevents message loss with the LEAST operational overhead.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements?",
