    question_en: "An organization is designing a high availability multi-tier web application architecture on AWS. The application consists of Amazon EC2 instances in private subnets behind an internet-facing Application Load Balancer (ALB) and an Amazon RDS PostgreSQL database. The EC2 instances require outbound internet connectivity to download operating system updates and security patches. The architecture must eliminate all single points of failure and provide automated database failover with minimal recovery time.\n\nWhich architecture meets these requirements?",
