    question_en: "A nationwide retail company operates hundreds of physical stores. Every night after closing, each store uploads a compressed inventory audit file (approximately 200 MB) to central storage. The company needs these files to be processed automatically as soon as they are uploaded to update inventory records stored in an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database. In addition, store managers and supply chain analysts run heavy reporting queries and dashboards during morning business hours, which creates high CPU utilization and slows down transactional updates on the primary RDS DB instance.\n\nWhich combination of steps should a solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements with the least operational overhead?",
