    question_en: "A global logistics company tracks thousands of international cargo shipments daily. Delivery vehicles and regional logistics hubs capture high-resolution shipment verification videos and sensor telemetry packages (averaging 500 MB to 2 GB per manifest) that must be uploaded from locations worldwide to AWS. Once uploaded, a batch data processing pipeline runs overnight within a 6-hour window to index and analyze the video footage. The batch analytics workload is stateless, parallelized, and fault-tolerant, with built-in checkpointing that allows jobs to resume if interrupted.\n\nThe company requires a solution that minimizes upload latency for global hubs, maximizes compute cost efficiency for the overnight batch processing, and adheres to AWS security best practices for instance permissions.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements?",
