    question_en: "A regional airline, Skylark Express, is modernizing its flight reservation and passenger check-in web portal. The portal experiences unpredictable traffic spikes during holiday flash sales and requires Layer 7 path-based routing to separate standard flight searches from the passenger check-in workflow. During online check-in, passengers upload scanned travel identification documents and baggage dimension photos, which must be durably stored and accessible only to internal verification systems. To maintain high availability and reliability, the web tier must scale dynamically across multiple Availability Zones (AZs) without storing local session or file state on the servers, and must interact with storage securely without hardcoded credentials.\n\nWhich architecture should a solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements with the least operational overhead?",
