    question_en: "A regional airline operates a flight booking web application using Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer and a single-AZ Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database. During seasonal promotional campaigns, millions of users search for flight schedules and fare classes (read traffic), which causes severe database performance degradation and delays ticket purchase transactions (write traffic). Furthermore, the airline requires high availability with automated failover in the event of an Availability Zone outage.\n\nWhich combination of actions will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?",
