    question_en: "An organization operates a backend service that processes incoming batch transaction records submitted via an internal API. The transaction volume is highly intermittent and unpredictable throughout the day, with each processing task completing in under 5 seconds. The workload currently runs on a fleet of always-on Amazon EC2 instances that write to an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database. To prevent connection exhaustion errors caused by concurrent worker connections during peak spikes, the organization significantly overprovisioned the RDS DB instance to a large instance size, resulting in high idle infrastructure costs.\n\nA solutions architect must redesign the architecture to handle the unpredictable traffic spikes, minimize compute and database idle costs, and prevent database connection exhaustion with the least operational overhead.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements?",
