    question_en: "A company hosts a web application on Amazon EC2 instances that experience unpredictable HTTP and HTTPS traffic spikes. The architecture requires routing incoming requests to different backend services based on the URL path (`/api/*` and `/images/*`). In addition, the solution must automatically scale EC2 capacity to handle fluctuating traffic loads, ensure high availability across multiple Availability Zones, and automatically replace instances if the application process becomes unresponsive, even if the underlying virtual machine remains operational.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?",
