    question_en: "An organization hosts a stateless web service on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer across multiple Availability Zones. The service requires a continuous baseline capacity of 4 instances running 24/7 to handle normal traffic. During irregular traffic surges, the service must scale up to 20 instances to maintain performance. The application is stateless and resilient to instance interruptions for the surge capacity. A solutions architect needs to design a solution that automatically scales to maintain an average CPU utilization of 50% while minimizing compute costs.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements MOST cost-effectively?",
