    question_en: "A company runs a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances hosting a stateful application. The operations team discovers that background worker threads intermittently cause system memory exhaustion, leading to application crashes. The company wants an automated solution that monitors OS-level memory utilization across all instances in near-real time. When memory utilization exceeds 85% for 5 consecutive minutes, the solution must immediately execute a remediation script to safely restart the background worker service on the affected instance without terminating or rebooting the instance.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?",
