    question_en: "A university manages an online learning portal where web traffic fluctuates unpredictably, peaking sharply during course registration and final exam periods. In addition, students upload short video, audio, and document submissions (each under 5 minutes in duration and taking less than 1 minute to process) to an Amazon S3 bucket. The university needs to extract metadata and convert submitted media files into standardized formats immediately upon upload. Currently, both the web application and background file processing run on a fixed set of standalone Amazon EC2 instances, causing performance degradation during peak traffic.\n\nA solutions architect must design a highly scalable and cost-effective architecture that handles unpredictable web traffic and processes uploaded files with the least operational overhead.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements?",
