    question_en: "A company hosts a web application on Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group behind an Application Load Balancer. The application receives unpredictable traffic spikes and accepts two types of processing jobs from users:\n1. Lightweight metadata extraction jobs that finish in under 10 seconds.\n2. Complex batch computation jobs that require 25 to 40 minutes of continuous execution.\n\nThe company must decouple the web tier from the processing backend to prevent request loss during spikes. The solution must minimize operational overhead and idle costs for the lightweight jobs, and run the long-running batch jobs in the most cost-effective manner.\n\nWhich architecture meets these requirements?",
